{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/434", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"can I adjust the widgets layout in the wp-admin\", \"response\": \"Yes, you can adjust the widgets layout in the WordPress admin area. Here are the steps to do it:\\n\\n1. Go to the Appearance section in the WordPress admin area.\\n2. Click on the Widgets option.\\n3. You will see a list of available widgets on the right side of the screen.\\n4. Click and drag the widgets to the areas where you want to display them on your website. You can add widgets to the sidebars, footers, and other areas of your website.\\n5. You can also adjust the settings of each widget by clicking on the widget and making changes in the settings panel on the right side of the screen.\\n6. Once you have added and arranged the widgets as you want, click on the Save button to apply the changes to your website.\\n\\nNote: The exact steps and options may vary depending on your WordPress theme and the widgets that are available. However, the general process of adding and arranging widgets in the WordPress admin area is similar across most themes and plugins.\\n\\nIf you need more specific instructions or have any questions about adjusting the widgets layout in the WordPress admin area, feel free to ask. I'm here to help!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned wit