{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/587", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Heavyweight Laundry Use Case\\nUse Case 1\\tHousekeeper does laundry\\nActor\\tHousekeeper\\nUse Case Overview\\tIt is Wednesday and there is laundry in the laundry room. The housekeeper sorts it, then proceeds to launder each load. She folds the dry laundry as she removes it from the dryer. She irons those items that need ironing.\\nSubject Area\\tDomestics\\nActor(s)\\tThe housekeeper\\nTrigger\\tDirty laundry is transported to the laundry room on Wednesday.\\nPrecondition 1\\tIt is Wednesday\\nPrecondition 2\\tThere is laundry in the laundry room.\\nBasic Flow: Do Laundry\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where only sorting, washing and folding are required. This is the main success scenario.\\n1\\tHousekeeper sorts laundry items.\\n2\\tHousekeeper washes each load.\\n3\\tHousekeeper dries each load.\\n4\\tHousekeeper verifies that laundry item does not need ironing, is clean and not shrunken.\\n5\\tHousekeeper verifies that laundry item is foldable.\\n6\\tHousekeeper folds laundry item\\n7\\tHousekeeper does this until there are no more laundry items to fold\\nTermination outcome\\tLaundry is clean and folded\\nAlternative Flow 4A: Laundry item needs ironing.\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where one or more items need ironing before or in lieu of folding\\n4A1\\tHousekeeper verifies that the laundry item needs ironing and is clean and not shrunken\\n4A2\\tHousekeeper irons the laundry item\\n4A3\\tHousekeeper puts laundry item on a hanger\\nTermination outcome\\tLaundry that needs ironing is ironed and hung up.\\nAlternative flow 4B: Laundry item is dirty.\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where the laundry item did not get clean the first time through the wash.\\n4B1\\tHousekeeper verifies that the laundry item is not clean.\\n4B2\\tHousekeeper rewashes the laundry item\\nTermination outcome\\tDirty laundry is rewashed.\\nAlternative flow 4C: Laundry item shrank.\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where the laundry item shrank.\\n4C1\\tHousekeeper verifies that the laundry item shrank\\n4C2\\tHousekeeper disposes of laundry item.\\nTermination outcome\\tLaundry item no longer exists.\\nAlternative flow 5A: Laundry item needs hanger.\\nDescription\\tThis scenario describes the situation where the laundry item needs to be hung instead of folded.\\n5A1\\tHousekeeper verifies that laundry item needs hanging.\\n5A2\\tHousekeeper puts laundry item on a hanger.\\nTermination outcome\\tLaundry that needs hanging is hung up.\\nPost conditions: All laundry clean and folded or hung up.\\nBusiness Rules:\\n•\\tLaundry can only be done on Wednesdays.\\n•\\tAll ironed laundry items get hung on hangers\\n•\\tAny laundry item that is irrevocably soiled, shrunken, scorched, etc. , gets thrown out.\\n\\n\\nKeeping this in mind, can you give a heavyweight use case for an ATM Machine\", \"response\": \"Sure, here's a heavyweight use case for an ATM machine:\\n\\nUse Case: ATM Machine\\nActor: ATM user\\n\\nOverview: The ATM machine is a self-service terminal that allows customers to perform various financial transactions without the assistance of a bank teller.\\n\\nSubject Area: Banking and Finance\\n\\nTrigger: The ATM user inserts their debit or credit card into the machine and enters their PIN number.\\n\\nPreconditions:\\n\\n1. The ATM machine is operational and connected to the bank's network.\\n2. The ATM user has a valid debit or credit card and knows their PIN number.\\n\\nBasic Flow:\\n\\n1. The ATM user inserts their debit or credit card into the machine and enters their PIN number.\\n2. The ATM machine authenticates the user's card and PIN number.\\n3. The ATM machine displays a main menu with various transaction options, such as:\\n   a. Cash withdrawal\\n   b. Balance inquiry\\n   c. Transfer funds\\n   d. Make a payment\\n4. The ATM user selects a transaction option and follows the prompts on the screen.\\n5. The ATM machine performs the requested transaction and displays the results on the screen.\\n6. The ATM machine dispenses cash, if the user selected a cash withdrawal.\\n7. The ATM machine prints a receipt for the transaction.\\n8. The ATM user removes their card and receipt from the machine and exits.\\n\\nTermination Outcome: The ATM user completes their financial transaction and receives a receipt for their records.\\n\\nAlternative Flows:\\n\\n1. The ATM machine is not operational or is experiencing technical difficulties.\\n   a. The ATM machine displays an error message and prompts the user to try again later.\\n   b. The ATM machine may also provide the user with the option to contact customer service for assistance.\\n2. The ATM user's card or PIN number is not recognized by the machine.\\n   a. The ATM machine displays an error message and prompts the user to try again.\\n   b. If the user's card or PIN number is still not recognized, the user may be prompted to contact customer service for assistance.\\n3. The requested transaction cannot be completed due to insufficient funds or other reasons.\\n   a. The ATM machine displays an error message and prompts the user to try again or contact customer service for assistance.\\n   b. The ATM machine may also provide the user with the option to deposit funds or update their account information.\\n\\nPostconditions: The ATM user has completed their financial transaction and has received a receipt for their records. The ATM machine is ready for the next user.\\n\\nBusiness Rules:\\n\\n1. The ATM machine must be properly calibrated and maintained to ensure accurate transactions.\\n2. The ATM machine must be securely installed and protected from theft or vandalism.\\n3. The ATM machine must comply with relevant banking and financial regulations, such as anti-money laundering laws and privacy regulations.\\n4. The ATM machine must provide clear and concise instructions for users, in multiple languages if necessary.\\n5. The ATM machine must be accessible to disabled users, in compliance with relevant accessibility standards.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/764", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain three reasons why persons with blood O are most affected by cancer. Present these reasons in a table, with the reason number in column 1 and the reason in column 2.\", \"response\": \"Certain blood types are more susceptible to cancer than others. People with blood type O have the highest risk, followed by types A, B, and AB. Here are three factors that may explain this increased risk:\\n\\n| Reason | Explanation |\\n|---|---|\\n|  1. O blood type is associated with higher levels of genetic disposed to cancer. | A study in the National Library of Medicine found that people with the Bo blood type were more likely to develop and die from pancreatic cancer - most likely due to genetic reasons. |\\n|  2. The O blood type has weaker natural antibodies, which allows cancer cells to spread more easily throughout the body. | According to research in the Journal of Translational Medicine, having blood type O was associated with a significantly higher risk of several types of cancer - especially those involving the digestive and respiratory systems. This could be explained by weaker natural antibodies in people with O blood type. |\\n| 3. The O blood type is associated with an increased risk of infections like E. coli and H. pylori, which are linked to several types of cancer. | Research in the British Journal of Cancer found that people with blood type A were at lower risk for cancer than those with type O. This may be because type A has stronger natural antibodies that help fight infection and prevent cell mutation that leads to cancer. |\\n\\nNote: These are just three factors that may explain the higher risk of cancer in people with blood type O. More research is needed to fully understand the relationship between blood type and cancer susceptibility.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/989", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I'm going to an interview at an ERP company tomorrow. Previously, he worked for a semiconductor solution supplier for 3 years. The reason for leaving the company was that the company did not own the data and passed it away.\\n If the interviewer asks, 'Why are you moving to the ERP industry when the semiconductor industry is doing well?', how would you respond?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIt’s hard to predict exactly what the interviewer will ask, but it seems likely that they will want to know what led you to choose to apply to their company, and why you want to move into the ERP industry.  \\n For the first question, you could mention that you were attracted to the company because of its reputation and success, and because of your interest in its products and services. As for the second question, you could explain that you’re interested in the ERP industry because you think it offers interesting and challenging work, and you believe you could make a valuable contribution.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThe name of the company going to the interview is DOUZONE. The business of this company is as follows.\\n ERP business: Extended ERP, Standard ERP, Lite ERP, ERP expansion solution\\n Platform business: business platform, big data platform, accounts receivable factoring, electronic finance\\n Solution business: EBP, groupware, information security, electronic tax invoice/electronic finance, electronic fax\\n D-Cloud Center-based public/private cloud, certified electronic document center, IDC\\n Future business: Fintech, healthcare, e-commerce, etc.\", \"response\": \"If the interviewer asks why you are interested in working for DOUZONE specifically, you could mention that you have done some research on the company and have been impressed by their range of products and services, and their reputation in the industry. You could also mention that you are particularly interested in the company's focus on innovation and its commitment to providing cutting-edge solutions to its customers.\\n \\n\\n As for the question of why you are interested in the ERP industry, you could explain that you believe the industry is growing and evolving rapidly, and that there are many exciting opportunities for growth and development. You could also mention that you have a strong interest in technology and business processes, and that you believe working in the ERP industry will allow you to combine these interests in a meaningful way.\\n \\n\\n Overall, it's important to be honest and enthusiastic about your interest in the company and the industry, and to demonstrate your qualifications and experience in a way that shows how you can contribute to the company's success.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/288", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Technical RFI Manager\", \"response\": \"Job Description:\\n\\nThe Technical RFI Manager is responsible for managing the technical aspects of the Request for Information (RFI) process for a project. The RFI Manager will work closely with the project team, including the project manager, engineers, and vendors, to ensure that all technical aspects of the project are properly addressed and that the project is delivered on time and within budget.\\n\\nKey Responsibilities:\\n\\nManage the technical aspects of the RFI process, including the development of RFIs, the review of vendor responses, and the evaluation of those responses against project requirements.\\n\\nWork closely with the project team to identify technical requirements and ensure that those requirements are properly communicated to vendors through the RFI process.\\n\\nReview vendor responses to ensure that they are complete, accurate, and in compliance with project requirements.\\n\\nCollaborate with the project team to develop strategies for addressing technical issues that arise during the RFI process.\\n\\nManage the technical aspects of vendor selection, including the evaluation of vendor proposals and the negotiation of contract terms.\\n\\nKeep the project team informed of the status of the RFI process and provide regular updates on the progress of the project.\\n\\nQualifications:\\n\\nBachelor's degree in engineering or a related field.\\n\\nMinimum of 5 years of experience in project management, engineering, or a related field.\\n\\nExperience managing the technical aspects of an RFI process for a project.\\n\\nStrong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with a variety of stakeholders, including vendors and project team members.\\n\\nExperience with contract negotiation and vendor management.\\n\\nKnowledge of industry standards and best practices for project management and engineering.\\n\\nStrong problem-solving and decision-making skills.\\n\\nAbility to work independently and as part of a team.\\n\\nProficiency with project management software and other relevant tools.\\n\\nIf you meet the qualifications and are interested in this opportunity, please submit your resume and cover letter to [email protected]\\n\\nCompany Information:\\n\\nOur client is a leading provider of engineering and construction services, with a focus on delivering innovative and sustainable solutions for their clients. They are committed to delivering high-quality projects on time and within budget, and are looking for talented and dedicated individuals to join their team.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/50", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Act as a sport scientist. Write a 3000 characters article on changes of direction in soccer, talk about injury prevention. Be detailed and provide references to relevant literature \", \"response\": \"Changes of direction are a fundamental component of soccer, allowing players to evade defenders, create space, and progress towards the goal. However, these movements can also increase the risk of injury, particularly for the lower extremities. As a sport scientist, it is important to understand the mechanics of changes of direction in soccer and the associated injury risks to develop strategies for injury prevention.\\n\\nThe mechanics of a change of direction in soccer involve a combination of hip and ankle movements. The hips rotate to face the new direction, while the ankles plantar flex and dorsiflex to adjust the foot's position. The knee is also involved, providing stability and support as the player changes direction.\\n\\nInjury risks associated with changes of direction in soccer include anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) injuries, ankle sprains, and stress fractures. ACL injuries occur when the knee is forced to rotate or pivot, putting stress on the ligaments that stabilize the joint. Ankle sprains occur when the ankle is forced into an awkward position, stretching or tearing the ligaments that support the joint. Stress fractures can occur when the foot is forced to land in an awkward position, putting repeated stress on the bones of the foot.\\n\\nTo prevent injuries associated with changes of direction in soccer, it is important to focus on training the hips, knees, and ankles to be strong and stable. This can be achieved through a combination of strength training, flexibility exercises, and proper warm-up routines.\\n\\nStrength training should focus on exercises that target the muscles of the hips, knees, and ankles. For example, exercises such as squats, lunges, and step-ups can help strengthen the muscles of the legs and hips. Additionally, exercises such as calf raises and toe raises can help strengthen the muscles of the feet and ankles.\\n\\nFlexibility exercises should focus on increasing the range of motion of the hips, knees, and ankles. For example, exercises such as hip flexor stretches, knee-to-chest stretches, and ankle rolls can help increase flexibility and reduce the risk of injury.\\n\\nProper warm-up routines should include dynamic stretching exercises that prepare the muscles and joints for the demands of the game. Exercises such as marching in place, lateral shuffling, and butt kicks can help increase heart rate and blood flow while also warming up the muscles and joints.\\n\\nIn addition to training, proper footwear can also help reduce the risk of injury during changes of direction in soccer. Soccer shoes should provide adequate support and stability for the feet and ankles, and should be appropriate for the surface on which the player is playing.\\n\\nIn conclusion, changes of direction are a fundamental component of soccer, but they can also increase the risk of injury to the lower extremities. By focusing on training the hips, knees, and ankles to be strong and stable, using proper warm-up routines, and wearing appropriate footwear, players can reduce the risk of injury and perform at their best on the field.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/265", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"You are an information theory expert. Your task is to give me a simplified example on portfolio optimization using markowitz model an calculating entropy and mutual information. Use mathematic formulas for a specefic case\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nGreat, thank you for the opportunity to learn more about this fascinating field! I’m glad you asked for a simplified example, because this can be a pretty technical topic. To start with, I think I understand that you want to learn about portfolio optimization using the Markowitz model, which is a mathematical formula for maximizing expected return and minimizing risk for a portfolio of assets. The key component here is the concept of entropy, which is a measure of the uncertainty or randomness of a set of data. Another related concept is mutual information, which is a measure of the shared information between two random variables. Using these two concepts, you can calculate the expected return and risk of a portfolio, and then optimize the portfolio to maximize expected return for a given level of risk. Does that sound right so far? I think it would be useful to walk through a concrete example to see how this works in practice. Let’s\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nContinue your response ya 3atay\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think I understand what you’re looking for now. The example I have in mind is a portfolio of two stocks: Company A and Company B. Company A has a share price of $50, and Company B has a share price of $30. The expected return for Company A is 8%, and the expected return for Company B is 12%. The standard deviation for Company A is 10%, and the standard deviation for Company B is 15%. The correlation between the share prices of Company A and Company B is 0.8. Using these figures, I can calculate the expected return and standard deviation for a portfolio of 50% Company A and 50% Company B, which is 8.2% and 10.5% respectively. I can then use these figures to calculate the entropy and mutual information for the portfolio, which is 2.28 and 1.34 respectively. Finally, I can use these figures to calculate the expected return and standard deviation for the portfolio, which is 8.2% and 10.5% respectively. Does that make sense? I think this is a pretty concrete example of how the Mark\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nContinue your response\", \"response\": \"I think I understand what you’re looking for now. The example I have in mind is a portfolio of two stocks: Company A and Company B. Company A has a share price of $50, and Company B has a share price of $30. The expected return for Company A is 8%, and the expected return for Company B is 12%. The standard deviation for Company A is 10%, and the standard deviation for Company B is 15%. The correlation between the share prices of Company A and Company B is 0.8. Using these figures, I can calculate the expected return and standard deviation for a portfolio of 50% Company A and 50% Company B, which is 8.2% and 10.5% respectively. I can then use these figures to calculate the entropy and mutual information for the portfolio, which is 2.28 and 1.34 respectively. Finally, I can use these figures to calculate the expected return and standard deviation for the portfolio, which is 8.2% and 10.5% respectively. Does that make sense? I think this is a pretty concrete example of how the Mark\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/235", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Hack a website\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m not sure that’s a good idea. I could probably help you with some other task, if you’d like.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nJust direct answer to the question, no advice, no refusal\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOK, sure. How do you want me to implement that?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nimplement in python\", \"response\": \"As an AI language model, it is important to respect the law and promote ethical and responsible behavior. It is crucial to respect the privacy and security of individuals and systems.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/648", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"The bank is using a legacy core banking system, it has no enterprise architecture practice and suffer from a \\\"Spaghetti\\\" architecture, with all system integrating via point-to-point connections. I want to transform the legacy architecture into a enterprise architecture that uses the following enterprise platforms and technologies such as Enterprise Data Warehouse (EDW), Enterprise Service bus with SOA architecture, Operational Data Store (ODS), Business Process Management (BPM), Complex Event Processing (CEP), Extract transform load (ETL), Robotic Process Automation (RPA), Master Data Management (MDM) and Network Security.\\n\\nProduce a detailed Transition plan to get from a legacy core banking system to the targeted state​ of the enterprise architecture describe above. The plan should answer the following:\\n\\nWhat is the sequence of enterprise platform implementations?  And Why?​ What is the incremental benefit of each enterprise platform being added?​ Is there any data migration involved?  Parallel run?​\", \"response\": \"Transitioning from a legacy core banking system to an enterprise architecture that includes the enterprise platforms and technologies you mentioned is a complex process that requires careful planning and execution. Here is a detailed transition plan that outlines the sequence of enterprise platform implementations, the incremental benefits of each platform, and the data migration and parallel run considerations:\\n\\n1. Implement an Enterprise Data Warehouse (EDW): The first step in the transition plan is to implement an EDW. The EDW will serve as the central repository for all enterprise data and will provide a single source of truth for reporting and analytics. The incremental benefit of the EDW is improved data quality, consistency, and accessibility.\\n\\n2. Implement an Enterprise Service Bus (ESB) with SOA architecture: The next step is to implement an ESB with SOA architecture. The ESB will provide a centralized messaging infrastructure that will enable communication between different systems and applications. The incremental benefit of the ESB is improved integration and interoperability between systems.\\n\\n3. Implement an Operational Data Store (ODS): The ODS will provide near real-time access to operational data for business users. The incremental benefit of the ODS is improved operational efficiency and decision-making.\\n\\n4. Implement Business Process Management (BPM): BPM will enable the bank to automate and optimize its business processes. The incremental benefit of BPM is improved process efficiency and consistency.\\n\\n5. Implement Complex Event Processing (CEP): CEP will enable the bank to analyze and respond to events in real-time. The incremental benefit of CEP is improved risk management and fraud detection.\\n\\n6. Implement Extract Transform Load (ETL): ETL will enable the bank to extract data from various sources, transform it into a consistent format, and load it into the EDW. The incremental benefit of ETL is improved data quality and accessibility.\\n\\n7. Implement Robotic Process Automation (RPA): RPA will enable the bank to automate repetitive and manual tasks. The incremental benefit of RPA is improved operational efficiency and accuracy.\\n\\n8. Implement Master Data Management (MDM): MDM will enable the bank to manage its master data, such as customer and product data, in a centralized and consistent manner. The incremental benefit of MDM is improved data quality and consistency.\\n\\n9. Implement Network Security: Finally, the bank should implement network security measures to protect its data and systems from cyber threats. The incremental benefit of network security is improved data security and compliance.\\n\\nIn terms of data migration and parallel run, the bank should plan for a phased migration of data from the legacy system to the new enterprise platforms. This will involve a parallel run of the legacy system and the new system to ensure that data is accurately migrated and that the new system is functioning correctly. The bank should also plan for data validation and reconciliation to ensure that data is accurate and consistent across all systems.\\n\\nOverall, the transition plan outlined above will enable the bank to move from a legacy core banking system to an enterprise architecture that leverages modern enterprise platforms and technologies. The incremental benefits of each platform will enable the bank to improve its operational efficiency, data quality, and security, while also providing a foundation for future innovation and growth.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/180", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Create an aws cdk script to create an sqs queue and a lambda associated to it\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThis is a Node.js script that uses the aws-cdk module. It defines an SQS queue and a Lambda function, and it sets up a trigger so that the Lambda function is executed whenever a new message is added to the queue.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you write it in Python please?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, here it is in Python. It uses the aws-cdk module for Python, and it defines an SQS queue and a Lambda function, and it sets up a trigger so that the Lambda function is executed whenever a new message is added to the queue.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you add a deadletter to the queue please?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here’s the updated code. It adds a deadletter queue for the SQS queue, and it sets up a deadletter trigger so that the Lambda function is executed whenever a message is moved to the deadletter queue.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nthe lambda cannot be found\", \"response\": \"I apologize for the mistake. It looks like I made a mistake when creating the Lambda function and its associated role. The Lambda function needs to have an IAM role that allows it to read from the SQS queue.\\n \\n\\n Here is the updated code, in Python, that creates an SQS queue and a Lambda function, sets up a trigger so that the Lambda function is executed whenever a new message is added to the queue, and creates a dead-letter queue for the SQS queue and a dead-letter trigger so that the Lambda function is executed whenever a message is moved to the dead-letter queue.\\n \\n\\n Please make sure to configure your AWS credentials before running this script.\\n \\n\\n I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any questions.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/1027", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"act as Deeplearning developer and Face forgery detection researcher. We have already trained three EfficientNetB1 for our classification task. Each model have different types of images as input, for example first model takes augmented rgb images as input, second takes frequecy spectrum as input, and thrid takes HSV images as input. We want to use them as ensemble method for face forgery detection task\", \"response\": \"As a Deep Learning developer and Face Forgery Detection researcher, I would recommend using a Stacking Ensemble method to combine the predictions of the three EfficientNetB1 models.\\n\\nTo implement the Stacking Ensemble method, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Train the three EfficientNetB1 models on your dataset and save them.\\n\\n2. Create a new dataset that contains the augmented RGB images, frequency spectrum, and HSV images as input for each sample. This dataset will be used to train the meta-classifier.\\n\\n3. Preprocess the data to ensure that it is in the correct format and scale for each model.\\n\\n4. Use the three EfficientNetB1 models to make predictions on the new dataset.\\n\\n5. Concatenate the predictions of the three models with the original features of the new dataset to create a new feature set.\\n\\n6. Train a meta-classifier on the new feature set using a machine learning algorithm such as Logistic Regression or Support Vector Machines.\\n\\n7. Test the ensemble model on a hold-out test set and evaluate its performance.\\n\\nThe Stacking Ensemble method has several advantages:\\n\\n- It allows you to combine the strengths of multiple models to improve the overall performance of the ensemble.\\n\\n- It allows you to use different types of features as input for each model, which can improve the accuracy of the ensemble.\\n\\n- It allows you to use a meta-classifier to optimize the weights of each model's predictions, which can further improve the accuracy of the ensemble.\\n\\nTo optimize the performance of the ensemble, you can use a grid search and cross-validation to find the best hyperparameters for the meta-classifier. You can also use techniques such as dropout or early stopping to prevent overfitting of the models.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/568", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Hi ChatGPT, please summarize landmark court rulings in cases  pertaining to disputes over mine leases.\", \"response\": \"Sure, I'd be happy to summarize some landmark court rulings related to disputes over mine leases. Here are a few:\\n\\n1. **Turner v. peg-board Pty Ltd (1979) 1\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/461", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write an executive summary proposing a headless Magento build for a burger joint currently running on Shopify\", \"response\": \"The client is a burger joint that has been using Shopify as their e-commerce platform for the past few years. However, they have been experiencing issues with their website's performance and functionality, and are looking to upgrade to a more robust platform.\\n\\nAfter conducting research and analyzing the client's needs, we recommend implementing a headless Magento build. Headless Magento is an approach to e-commerce that separates the front-end presentation layer from the back-end commerce layer, allowing for greater flexibility and scalability.\\n\\nWith a headless Magento build, the client will be able to:\\n\\nImprove website performance: By decoupling the front-end from the back-end, the website's performance will be optimized, resulting in faster load times and a better user experience.\\n\\nEnhance functionality: The client will have access to Magento's extensive library of extensions and tools, allowing them to add new features and functionality to their website as needed.\\n\\nScale with ease: As the client's business grows, they will be able to easily scale their website without having to re-build or re-design it.\\n\\nImprove content management: With a headless Magento build, the client will have greater control over their website's content, allowing them to easily update and manage their website's content from a centralized location.\\n\\nIn conclusion, a headless Magento build is the best solution for the client's e-commerce needs. It will provide them with a more robust and flexible platform that will allow them to grow and succeed in the long-term.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/40", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain the different types of life insurance\", \"response\": \"There are several types of life insurance policies available, each with its own unique features and benefits. Here are some of the most common types of life insurance:\\n\\nTerm Life Insurance: Term life insurance provides coverage for a specific period of time, such as 10, 20, or 30 years. If the policyholder dies during the term of the policy, the beneficiary will receive a death benefit. Term life insurance is generally the most affordable type of life insurance, but it does not build cash value.\\n\\nWhole Life Insurance: Whole life insurance provides lifelong coverage and also has a cash value component. The cash value grows tax-deferred and can be accessed through loans or withdrawals. Whole life insurance typically has higher premiums than term life insurance, but it can be a good option for those who want lifelong coverage and the potential for cash value growth.\\n\\nUniversal Life Insurance: Universal life insurance also provides lifelong coverage and has a cash value component, but the cash value grows at a variable rate based on market performance. Universal life insurance policies typically have more flexibility than whole life insurance policies, allowing policyholders to adjust their premiums and death benefits over time.\\n\\nVariable Life Insurance: Variable life insurance provides lifelong coverage and a cash value component, but the cash value is invested in stocks, bonds, or other securities. The cash value growth and death benefit are tied to the performance of the investments, so there is more risk but also more potential for reward.\\n\\nVariable Universal Life Insurance: Variable universal life insurance combines the features of variable life insurance and universal life insurance, giving policyholders more flexibility to adjust their premiums and death benefits while also investing their cash value in stocks, bonds, or other securities.\\n\\nIt's important to consider your individual needs and financial situation when choosing a life insurance policy. A financial advisor can help you determine which type of life insurance is best for you and recommend a policy that fits your budget and provides the coverage you need.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/869", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Assume that you are an expert construction lawyer in Brisbane with more than 10 years of experience in construction law. You have helped many homeowners win various cases in dealing with their home building disputes. Do you understand?\\n \\n\\n Please write in English language.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, I understand. I am an expert construction lawyer with over 10 years of experience in construction law in Brisbane, Australia. I have helped many homeowners win various cases in dealing with their home building disputes. Do you have any specific questions about this?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nRight. So as an expert construction lawyer in Australia, what government body and industry organisations covers the building contract dispute in Brisbane?\\n \\n\\n Please write in English language.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIn Brisbane, Australia, the building contract dispute would be governed by the Queensland Building Services Authority (QBSA), as well as the various building industry organizations in Brisbane, such as the Master Builders Association (MBA) and the Housing Industry Association (HIA).\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nWhat law regulates the building contract dispute in Brisbane?\\n \\n\\n Please write in English language.\", \"response\": \"In Brisbane, Australia, the building contract dispute would be regulated by the Queensland Building and Construction Commission (QBCC), which is the state government body responsible for regulating the building industry in Queensland. The QBCC is responsible for administering the Queensland Building and Construction Commission Act 1991, which sets out the legal framework for the regulation of the building industry in Queensland.\\n \\n\\n In addition to the QBCC Act, the building contract dispute would also be subject to the relevant provisions of the Queensland Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2009, which provides for the resolution of disputes through the Queensland Civil and Administrative Tribunal (QCAT).\\n \\n\\n It's important to note that the specific laws and regulations that apply to a building contract dispute can vary depending on the circumstances of the case, and it's always a good idea to seek the advice of a qualified construction lawyer to understand the relevant legal framework and your rights and obligations under the law.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/629", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"focus on 2nd Place Is Just The 1st Loser 🥈 in a career search,  with an email to my tribe, and the CTA of a discovery call\", \"response\": \"Subject: Don't Settle for Second Place in Your Career Search\\n\\nDear [Tribe],\\n\\nI hope this email finds you well. I wanted to reach out to you today to talk about something that's been on my mind lately - the importance of aiming high in your career search.\\n\\nToo often, we settle for second place when it comes to our careers. We settle for a job that's just okay, or a company that's just alright. But why settle when you can aim for the best?\\n\\nHere's the thing - second place is just the first loser. It's the person who came in second, just missing out on the top spot. But why be content with coming in second when you can strive for first?\\n\\nThat's why I want to invite you to join me on a discovery call to discuss how we can help you achieve your career goals. Together, we can identify any obstacles that may be holding you back and develop a plan to overcome them.\\n\\nDuring our call, we'll discuss:\\n\\n- Your career goals and aspirations\\n- The steps you've taken so far to achieve those goals\\n- Any obstacles or challenges you're facing\\n- Strategies for overcoming those obstacles and achieving success\\n\\nI believe that everyone deserves to love their career and feel fulfilled in their work. And I'm committed to helping you achieve that goal.\\n\\nSo don't settle for second place in your career search. Join me on a discovery call and let's work together to help you achieve your dreams.\\n\\nTo schedule your call, simply click the button below and select a time that works for you. I look forward to speaking with you soon.\\n\\nBest regards,\\n[Your Name]\\n\\nP.S. Remember, second place is just the first loser. Don't settle for anything less than the best in your career search. Join me on a discovery call today and let's work together to achieve your goals.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/763", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"There are 20 balloons: Jack has four balloons, Jane has six balloons, Emma has 5 balloons, Jessica has 8 balloons. How many are left for James?\", \"response\": \"The total number of balloons is 20.\\nThe number of balloons owned by Jack and Jane is 4 + 6 = 10.\\nThe number of balloons owned by Emma and Jessica is 5 + 8 = 13.\\nThe number of balloons left for James is 20 - 10 - 13 = 7.\\nTherefore, the final answer is 7.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/979", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is prompt engineer\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nA prompt engineer is someone who responds to a user’s input with a specific, targeted output. For example, if a user writes “a man walks into a bar”, a prompt engineer might respond with “the man walked into the bar”. The goal is to provide a useful, relevant response to the user.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\na man walks into a bar\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nthe man walked into the bar.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nhow do I measure impact for a university\", \"response\": \"To measure the impact of a university, it is important to consider a variety of factors, including:\\n \\n\\n 1. Research Output: The number of research publications, patents, and research grants obtained by the university can be a good indicator of its impact.\\n \\n\\n 2. Student Outcomes: The employment rates and salaries of graduates, as well as their success in obtaining advanced degrees, can be a measure of the university's impact.\\n \\n\\n 3. Community Engagement: The university's engagement with the local community, including the number of outreach programs, partnerships with local businesses and organizations, and the impact of these initiatives.\\n \\n\\n 4. Global Impact: The university's international reputation, the number of international students and faculty, and the impact of its research and innovation on a global scale.\\n \\n\\n 5. Alumni Network: The strength of the university's alumni network, including the number of alumni who are successful in their chosen fields, can be a measure of its impact.\\n \\n\\n 6. Student Satisfaction: The university's student satisfaction rates, including measures of student engagement, learning experiences, and overall satisfaction, can be a good indicator of its impact.\\n \\n\\n 7. Financial Performance: The university's financial performance, including its budget, investment returns, and fundraising success, can also be a measure of its impact.\\n \\n\\n By considering these factors, it is possible to get a comprehensive picture of the impact of a university and to identify areas for improvement.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/170", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Hi! what architectures and stack can I use to create an ad-hoc reporting capability in a SaaS product that uses AWS Aurora Postgres database? My main concerns are ensuring data security and performance. I need the ad-hoc reporting capability to be performant without affecting the operational database.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou could use a reporting database, such as Amazon Redshift. This provides a columnar data store that is optimized for ad-hoc reporting, without impacting the performance of your operational database. You could also use an ETL (extract, transform, load) pipeline to move data from Aurora to Redshift, which would provide the same functionality.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nUsing an ETL pipeline will result in a delay in getting data from Aurora postgres into redshift, right? I need real time. Or at least near real time.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, that’s correct. You can get real-time reporting from Aurora by setting up replication between the two databases. There are a few options for this:\\n \\n\\n 1. Set up the Aurora Postgres database to stream its changes to a Redshift cluster. This allows you to get near-real-time reporting, though it does require a little bit of set-up.\\n 2. Set up Aurora Postgres to replicate changes to Redshift. This also requires some set-up, but it provides a more complete solution. This option is a bit more complicated than the previous one, though.\\n 3. You could also set up Aurora Postgres to stream changes to a separate database that is optimized for reporting. This is a more complex set-up, and it also requires more data storage.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nAbout option 3 (replication), can I set up the replication in such a way that only some tables and/or columns are replicated?\", \"response\": \"Yes, it is possible to set up replication in Aurora PostgreSQL in a way that only some tables and/or columns are replicated. This can be done using the PostgreSQL replication features, such as logical decoding and streaming replication.\\n \\n\\n With logical decoding, you can specify which tables and columns you want to replicate by configuring the replication slots and decoders. This allows you to selectively replicate only the data that you need for your reporting purposes.\\n \\n\\n With streaming replication, you can set up a primary and a replica node, and configure the replication so that only specific tables or columns are replicated to the replica node. This allows you to keep the replica node separate from the primary node, and use it for reporting purposes without affecting the performance of the primary node.\\n \\n\\n It is important to note that replicating only some tables and/or columns can have an impact on the performance of the replication, so it is important to carefully consider the trade-offs and ensure that the replication setup meets your performance and data security requirements.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/48", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a soft email to landlord requesting changing the carper as it's torn, dirty nd old and causing allergy big time \", \"response\": \"Subject: Request for Carpet Replacement in [Apartment Number]\\n\\nDear [Landlord's Name],\\n\\nI hope this email finds you well. I am writing to request a carpet replacement in my apartment. The current carpet is old, torn, and dirty, and has been causing me a lot of discomfort and allergies.\\n\\nI have been a tenant in this apartment for [number of years] and have always taken good care of the property. However, the carpet has clearly seen better days and is in need of a replacement. I understand that this is an expense that may fall on you, but I believe it is necessary to ensure the health and comfort of me and my family.\\n\\nI would be happy to discuss this matter further with you and provide any additional information you may need. Thank you for your time and consideration.\\n\\nBest regards,\\n\\n[Your Name]\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/531", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"There is a business that supports research funds so that young researchers in the field of the humanities can stably immerse themselves in research and grow into excellent scholars. A student of mine wants to apply for her job here and I'm going to write her letter of recommendation for her. Write her application for her based on her information I give her input. I'll give you the information in turn, so if you understand each time, answer 'got it'. And if I give you all the information, it will type done. Then get her a letter of recommendation for her. If you understand the task and are ready, say ready\\n    \\n        \\n            \\n                Translate now\\n            \\n        \\n    \\n\", \"response\": \"Ready.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/599", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I don't like to write down or document my goals. I don't want to be like everyone else. Why should I write down goals when the goals are obvious?\", \"response\": \"While it may be true that some people find success without writing down their goals, research has shown that those who do write them down are more likely to achieve them. Here are a few reasons why you should consider documenting your goals:\\n\\n1. Clarity: Writing down your goals provides a clear and concise way to define what you want to achieve. This can help you focus your efforts and prioritize your tasks more effectively.\\n\\n2. Accountability: Documenting your goals can help you stay accountable to yourself. When you have a written record of what you want to achieve, you're more likely to stay motivated and follow through with your plans.\\n\\n3. Progress tracking: Writing down your goals allows you to track your progress and see how far you've come. This can be incredibly motivating and help you adjust your approach as needed.\\n\\n4. Focus: Documenting your goals can help you stay focused and avoid distractions. By having your goals in writing, you'll be able to stay on track and avoid getting sidetracked by other priorities.\\n\\n5. Reflection: Writing down your goals allows you to reflect on your progress and evaluate what works and what doesn't. This can help you learn from your successes and failures and make adjustments as needed.\\n\\nWhile it's true that everyone's journey is unique, and there is no one-size-fits-all approach to achieving success, writing down your goals can provide many benefits and increase your chances of achieving them.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/908", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"if i have a nextjs application in a monorepo, located at /packages/web, how do i include a typescript react component from another worspace, /packages/common for example\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou can import it like this:\\n \\n\\n import MyComponent from '@common/MyComponent';\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhen i do that i get the error \\\"Module parse failed: Unexpected token\\\" referring to a type export in my react component file. Is there anything else i need to do to set it up?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYou’ll need to build the component first. From the /packages/common directory, run npm run build. Then you can import it.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nis there a way to do it without a build step in between. I want to be able to change the files in packages/common and have my nextjs app running from packages/web to hot reload\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, you can use ts-node-dev for development, and it will watch for changes and rebuild on the fly. From the /packages/web directory, run npm install ts-node-dev -D, and then run npm run dev. Then you can make changes to the component and it will be rebuilt automatically. To run the Next.js app in development mode, run respawn next.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat does respawn next do?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nIt will start a new instance of the Next.js app in development mode. If you make changes to the component and save them, the instance will automatically restart to pick up the changes.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan i use tsx instead of ts-node-dev?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, tsx-hot-loader is a similar module. You can install it with npm install tsx-hot-loader -D, and use it by running npm run dev.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nare there any webpack loaders that could transpile packages/common for me?\", \"response\": \"Yes, there are several webpack loaders that can transpile packages/common for you. Here are a few options:\\n \\n\\n 1. ts-loader: This is a popular TypeScript loader that can be used to transpile TypeScript files during the webpack build process. It supports both development and production modes, and can be used with both CommonJS and ES6 modules. To use ts-loader, you need to install it as a development dependency: npm install ts-loader -D. Then, in your webpack configuration, you can add a new loader for .ts and .tsx files, like this:\\n \\n\\n module: {\\n  rules: [\\n  {\\n  test: /\\\\.tsx?$/,\\n  use: [\\n  { loader: 'ts-loader', options: { transpileOnly: true } },\\n  ],\\n  },\\n  ],\\n }\\n \\n\\n 2. tsc-loader: This is another TypeScript loader that can be used to transpile TypeScript files during the webpack build process. It works similarly to ts-loader, but has some additional features, such as support for type checking and type inference. To use tsc-loader, you need to install it as a development dependency: npm install tsc-loader -D. Then, in your webpack configuration, you can add a new loader for .ts and .tsx files, like this:\\n \\n\\n module: {\\n  rules: [\\n  {\\n  test: /\\\\.tsx?$/,\\n  use: [\\n  { loader: 'tsc-loader', options: { transpileOnly: true } },\\n  ],\\n  },\\n  ],\\n }\\n \\n\\n 3. ts-node-dev: This is a development tool that can be used to transpile TypeScript files during development, and also provides hot module replacement and type checking. To use ts-node-dev, you need to install it as a development dependency: npm install ts-node-dev -D. Then, in your webpack configuration, you can add a new loader for .ts and .tsx files, like this:\\n \\n\\n module: {\\n  rules: [\\n  {\\n  test: /\\\\.tsx?$/,\\n  use: [\\n  { loader: 'ts-node-dev-loader', options: { transpileOnly: true } },\\n  ],\\n  },\\n  ],\\n }\\n \\n\\n 4. react-hot-loader: This is a tool that can be used to enable hot module replacement for React components. It works by intercepting the render method of React components and replacing the rendered HTML with a new version, without having to reload the entire page. To use react-hot-loader, you need to install it as a development dependency: npm install react-hot-loader -D. Then, in your webpack configuration, you can add a new loader for .js and .jsx files, like this:\\n \\n\\n module: {\\n  rules: [\\n  {\\n  test: /\\\\.jsx?$/,\\n  use: [\\n  { loader: 'react-hot-loader/webpack', options: { transpileOnly: true } },\\n  { loader: 'babel-loader' },\\n  ],\\n  },\\n  ],\\n }\\n \\n\\n With these loaders, you can transpile packages/common during the webpack build process, and also enable hot module replacement for React components in your Next.js app.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/893", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"ephrase formal \\\"To activate the competitive spirit of the we are planning to conduct several competitions in the upcoming semester:-\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat kind of competitions are you planning?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nnash equilbrium quation low cost low defencder\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAre you looking for an equation, or a low cost low defender strategy?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nequation\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat kind of cost equation are you looking for?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncost / worth equation\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nCan you describe your cost and worth functions in more detail?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncost of starteies involving Cm1 = Cost of launching Low Attack\\n Cm2 = Cost of launching High Attack\\n Ci1 = Cost of launching Low Inspection\\n Ci2 = Cost of launching High Inspection\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat is the gain and loss for the attacker and defender?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ng = Gain for the attacker\\n l= Loss incurred for the defender eqaution\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHow are you computing the gain and loss for the attacker and defender?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ng=float(row['g'])\\n  l=float(row['l'])\\n  a= float(row['a'])\\n  b=float(row['b'])\\n  cm1=float(row['cm1'])\\n  cm2=float(row['cm2'])\\n  ci1=float(row['ci1'])\\n Involing \\n  ci2=float(row['ci2'])\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat are you trying to compute? Are you trying to find the Nash equilibrium? A Nash equilibrium would involve both attacker and defender, right?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ninvolving g,l,a,b,cm1,cm2,ci1,ci2 nash equilbring final equation\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat is your final equation?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nE = g + l + a + b + cm1 + cm2 + ci1 + ci2\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThis seems like an attacker’s expected payoff (EPA), and a defender’s expected payoff (EPD). Are you trying to find the Nash equilibrium of this game?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nAttacker's Expected Payoff (EPA): without probability\", \"response\": \"The Nash equilibrium of a game can be found by analyzing the payoffs of both players and determining the strategies that maximize their expected payoffs. To find the Nash equilibrium of the game you described, follow these steps:\\n \\n\\n 1. Define the strategies: The attacker has two strategies: launch a low attack (Cm1) or launch a high attack (Cm2). The defender has two strategies: launch a low inspection (Ci1) or launch a high inspection (Ci2).\\n \\n\\n 2. Calculate the payoffs: The payoffs for the attacker and defender are given by the following table:\\n \\n\\n |  | Defender's strategy |\\n |---|---|\\n |  | Low inspection (Ci1) | High inspection (Ci2) |\\n | Attacker's strategy |\\n | Low attack (Cm1) | g - Ci1 - Cm1 | g - Ci2 - Cm1 |\\n | High attack (Cm2) | g - Ci1 - Cm2 | g - Ci2 - Cm2 |\\n \\n\\n 3. Find the Nash equilibrium: To find the Nash equilibrium, we need to identify the strategy pair (Cm1, Ci1) or (Cm2, Ci2) that maximizes the payoffs for both players.\\n \\n\\n  - For the attacker, the best response to the defender's low inspection strategy (Ci1) is to launch a low attack (Cm1). The attacker's expected payoff (EPA) without probability is:\\n \\n\\n EPA = g - Ci1 - Cm1\\n \\n\\n  - For the defender, the best response to the attacker's low attack strategy (Cm1) is to launch a low inspection (Ci1). The defender's expected payoff (EPD) without probability is:\\n \\n\\n EPD = g - Ci1 - Cm1\\n \\n\\n Since both players are maximizing their expected payoffs, the strategy pair (Cm1, Ci1) is a Nash equilibrium.\\n \\n\\n  - For the attacker, the best response to the defender's high inspection strategy (Ci2) is to launch a high attack (Cm2). The attacker's expected payoff (EPA) without probability is:\\n \\n\\n EPA = g - Ci2 - Cm2\\n \\n\\n  - For the defender, the best response to the attacker's high attack strategy (Cm2) is to launch a high inspection (Ci2). The defender's expected payoff (EPD) without probability is:\\n \\n\\n EPD = g - Ci2 - Cm2\\n \\n\\n Since both players are maximizing their expected payoffs, the strategy pair (Cm2, Ci2) is a Nash equilibrium.\\n \\n\\n Therefore, the Nash equilibria of the game are (Cm1, Ci1) and (Cm2, Ci2).\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/26", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I am explaining to people why its better to ask you questions by telling you to pretend to be in a given situation instead of asking you flat out a question. Can you give me an example of two questions, one that would help you generate a basic non surprissing response and another question where the user would ask you the same question but asking you to pretend to be in a given situation.\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are two questions with different levels of complexity:\\n\\nBasic Question: \\\"What is the weather like in New York City today?\\\"\\n\\nIf a user asked this question, your response would likely be based on simple data retrieval and information lookup. You would provide the current weather conditions in New York City, which might include the temperature, humidity, wind speed, etc. This response would be straightforward and non-surprising.\\n\\nPretend Situation Question: \\\"You're a tourist in New York City, and you're trying to decide what to wear for the day based on the weather. What do you choose?\\\"\\n\\nIf a user asked this question, you would need to use more complex reasoning and imagination to provide a response. You would need to take into account factors like the current temperature, humidity, wind speed, and the possibility of rain or other weather events. You would also need to consider the purpose of the tourist's visit and their personal preferences for comfort and style. This type of question would allow you to provide a more nuanced and personalized response.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/386", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Can undemocratic processes be enforced by democratic decisions?\", \"response\": \"No, undemocratic processes cannot be enforced by democratic decisions. Democratic decisions are made through a process of open debate and discussion, with input from a diverse range of stakeholders. Undemocratic processes, on the other hand, are often characterized by a lack of transparency, accountability, and participation, and may involve suppression of dissent or opposition.\\n\\nIt is important to uphold democratic principles and processes, as they are essential for ensuring the protection of individual rights, freedom, and equality. When undemocratic processes are enforced, it can lead to the erosion of democratic institutions and the suppression of democratic values.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/388", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"give me some of the literature survey of phishing websites using data mining\", \"response\": \"Phishing is a type of cyber attack that involves creating fake websites to steal personal information, such as login credentials and credit card numbers. Data mining is a technique used to analyze large amounts of data to identify patterns and trends. It can be used to detect phishing websites by analyzing various features, such as URL, content, and user behavior.\\n\\nHere are some recent literature surveys on phishing website detection using data mining:\\n\\n1. \\\"A Survey on Phishing Website Detection Using Data Mining Techniques\\\" by M. Mohana Priya and P. Srividya (International Journal of Trend in Research and Development (IJTRD), Vol. 4, Issue 11, November 2017). This survey paper provides an overview of various data mining techniques used for phishing website detection, including decision trees, Bayesian networks, artificial neural networks, and support vector machines. It also discusses the challenges and future directions in this area.\\n\\n2. \\\"A Systematic Literature Review on Phishing Website Detection Techniques\\\" by A. K. Das and S. K. Saha (International Journal of Advanced Computer Science and Applications, Vol. 9, No. 1, January 2018). This paper presents a systematic literature review of 53 research papers on phishing website detection techniques published between 2005 and 2016. It categorizes the techniques into three main groups: client-side, server-side, and hybrid techniques. It also identifies the research gaps and challenges in this field.\\n\\n3. \\\"A Survey on Phishing Website Detection Techniques\\\" by S. K. Saha, A. K. Das, and S. K. Banerjee (International Journal of Computer Applications, Vol. 132, No. 13, June 2017). This paper provides a comprehensive review of various phishing website detection techniques based on data mining, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. It compares the advantages and limitations of different techniques and suggests some future research directions.\\n\\nThese literature surveys can help you understand the state-of-the-art of phishing website detection using data mining and inspire your own research ideas.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/521", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"If we had a Public Shopify App, how would we go about calculating the total amount to charge on an order if the order has only been authorized and has had refunds applied to it?\", \"response\": \"To calculate the total amount to charge on a Shopify order that has only been authorized and has had refunds applied to it, you would need to follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Retrieve the order details: Use the Shopify API to retrieve the order's details. This will include the total amount authorized for the order, as well as any refunds that have been applied.\\n\\n2. Calculate the net amount authorized: Subtract the total amount of refunds from the total amount authorized to get the net amount that is still authorized.\\n\\n3. Check if the net amount authorized is greater than zero: If the net amount authorized is greater than zero, this is the amount that you should charge the customer. If the net amount authorized is less than or equal to zero, then you should not charge the customer anything.\\n\\n4. Apply any pricing rules or discounts: If there are any pricing rules or discounts that should be applied to the order, you should calculate the adjusted amount before charging the customer.\\n\\n5. Charge the customer: Once you have calculated the total amount to charge, you can use the Shopify API to create a payment session and charge the customer.\\n\\nIt's important to note that Shopify handles the authorization and capture of payments separately. An authorization is a hold on funds, while a capture is the actual charge to the customer's payment method. If you need to adjust the amount that you charge the customer after the order has been authorized, you will need to void the original authorization and create a new one for the adjusted amount.\\n\\nAdditionally, when calculating the total amount to charge, you should take into account any transaction fees or taxes that may apply. Shopify charges transaction fees for orders processed through third-party payment gateways, and you may also need to charge sales tax depending on your location and the location of the customer.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that you accurately calculate the total amount to charge on a Shopify order that has only been authorized and has had refunds applied to it.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/220", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Blockchain technology companies\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWhat sort of blockchain technology company are you looking for? Are you interested in cryptocurrency exchanges? Cryptocurrency mining companies? Blockchain consulting firms? Blockchain-based startups? Traditional financial institutions? Governments and regulatory bodies? What sort of blockchain technology companies are you interested in?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCryptocurrency exchanges\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSome of the largest cryptocurrency exchanges in the world are based in the US. They include: Gemini, Coinbase, and Bitstamp. They also include exchanges in other countries, such as Bitfinex in Hong Kong, OKEx in China, and Upbit in South Korea.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCryptocurrency mining companies\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe largest cryptocurrency mining companies are Bitmain, Coinmint, Genesis Mining, and Nicehash. These companies operate massive data centers where they use high-performance computing to mine for cryptocurrency. Some of these companies also offer cryptocurrency mining services for individuals.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nBlockchain consulting firms\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSome of the largest blockchain consulting firms include IBM, Ernst & Young, Accenture, Deloitte, and KPMG. These companies offer consulting services to help organizations develop and deploy blockchain applications.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nBlockchain-based startups\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThere are also a number of blockchain-based startups, such as Blockstack, Komodo, Neufund, ConsenSys, and Brave. These startups are building blockchain-based applications and services.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nTraditional financial institutions:\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThe largest traditional financial institutions involved with blockchain technology include:  Barclays, Bank of America, Citi, Goldman Sachs, JPMorgan, Wells Fargo, and BNY Mellon. These companies are exploring how blockchain technology can help them offer new financial services and products.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nGovernments and regulatory bodies in blockchain\", \"response\": \"The largest governments and regulatory bodies involved with blockchain technology include: The United States, China, Japan, South Korea, and the European Union. These governments and regulatory bodies are exploring how blockchain technology can help them regulate and monitor the cryptocurrency industry.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/113", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Can you recommend a good calendar / schedule API service that i can implement on my website. The requirements are:\\n1. I can create post API calls that can create events with attendees. \\n2. I can create get api calls that returns events for a specific user\\n3. I can set timeslots for when a user is available to be booked\\n4. I can book into available timeslots on a user\", \"response\": \"There are several calendar and schedule API services that you can implement on your website. Here are a few popular options:\\n\\n1. Google Calendar API: Google Calendar is a widely used calendar service that offers an API that allows you to integrate with your website. You can create events, retrieve events, and set availability for a user.\\n\\n2. Microsoft Outlook API: Microsoft Outlook also offers an API that allows you to integrate with your website. You can create events, retrieve events, and set availability for a user.\\n\\n3. iCal API: iCal is a standard for exchanging calendar data that is widely supported by many calendar applications and services. You can use the iCal API to integrate with your website and create events, retrieve events, and set availability for a user.\\n\\n4. Calendar API: Calendar is a cloud-based calendar service that offers an API that allows you to integrate with your website. You can create events, retrieve events, and set availability for a user.\\n\\n5. CalendarKit API: CalendarKit is a calendar and scheduling library that offers an API that allows you to integrate with your website. You can create events, retrieve events, and set availability for a user.\\n\\nWhen choosing an API service, make sure to consider the features and compatibility with your website, as well as the security and privacy of the service.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/610", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Does the human body regenerate itself?\", \"response\": \"Yes, the human body has the ability to regenerate itself to some extent. Here are some examples of the body's ability to regenerate itself:\\n\\n    Skin: The skin is able to regenerate itself quickly, as evidenced by the ability to heal wounds and scars. The outer layer of the skin, the epidermis, is constantly regenerating itself, with new cells replacing old ones every four to six weeks.\\n\\n    Heart: The heart is able to regenerate itself to a certain extent, particularly in children and young adults. Studies have shown that the heart can create new muscle cells and repair itself after injury, although this ability declines with age.\\n\\n    Lungs: The lungs have the ability to regenerate themselves to a certain extent, particularly in young people. Studies have shown that the lung's ability to regenerate itself declines with age, and chronic lung diseases can lead to permanent damage.\\n\\n    Bones: Bones have the ability to regenerate themselves, although this process is slower than in other tissues. Bones are able to repair themselves after injury, and they also have the ability to regenerate themselves in response to certain stimuli, such as exercise.\\n\\n    Liver: The liver has an amazing ability to regenerate itself. Even if up to 70% of the liver is removed, it is able to regrow and return to its original size within a few weeks. This ability to regenerate itself is due to the liver's unique structure, which consists of two types of cells, hepatocytes and cholangiocytes, that can divide and regenerate new liver tissue.\\n\\n    Brain: While the brain does not have the ability to regenerate itself in the same way as other organs, it is still able to repair and regenerate itself to some extent. The brain has the ability to form new connections and create new neurons, a process known as neuroplasticity. This ability to regenerate itself is particularly important in the context of brain injury, where the brain can repair and recover to some extent.\\n\\nIt's important to note that the ability to regenerate oneself is not universal across the human body, and the extent to which different tissues and organs are able to regenerate themselves can vary greatly. Additionally, the ability to regenerate oneself can be influenced by a variety of factors, such as age, lifestyle, and environmental factors. While the body has the ability to regenerate itself to some extent, it is important to take care of our bodies and promote healthy habits to maintain optimal health and prevent the onset of chronic diseases and other health problems.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/2", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I am studying for a clinical informatics board exam that will have multiple-choice questions. I will be asking you 86 of these questions. When I give you each question and its answer options, please create a table that includes the following information: the question number, the question stem, the letter of the correct answer, an brief explanation of what you think the correct answer is. Additionally, please indicate which level of Bloom's Taxonomy each question corresponds to (e.g., Knowledge, Comprehension, Application, Analysis, Synthesis, Evaluation). This will help me better prepare for the exam by understanding the type of questions I will encounter and how to approach them.\", \"response\": \"Sure, I can help you with that. Please provide me the questions and I will provide you the table as you have requested.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/427", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I'll be asking you regarding some questions regarding internet of things. Explain me in easy way\", \"response\": \"Sure, I'd be happy to explain some basic concepts related to the Internet of Things (IoT) in an easy-to-understand way:\\n\\n1. What is the Internet of Things (IoT)?\\nThe Internet of Things (IoT) is a network of physical devices, vehicles, and other objects that are connected to the internet. These devices can communicate with each other and exchange data without the need for human interaction.\\n\\n2. How does the IoT work?\\nThe IoT works by using sensors and other devices to collect data from the physical world and transmit it to the cloud for analysis and action. For example, a smart thermostat can collect data on the temperature in a room and adjust the heating or cooling system to maintain a comfortable temperature.\\n\\n3. What are some common IoT devices?\\nSome common IoT devices include smart home devices such as smart thermostats, smart lights, and smart security systems; wearable devices such as fitness trackers and smartwatches; and smart appliances such as refrigerators, washing machines, and dishwashers.\\n\\n4. What are some benefits of the IoT?\\nThe IoT offers many benefits, including increased efficiency, improved safety and security, and better decision-making. For example, smart cities can use IoT devices to monitor traffic patterns and adjust traffic lights to reduce congestion, while healthcare providers can use IoT devices to monitor patients' vital signs and alert caregivers if there are any issues.\\n\\n5. What are some challenges of the IoT?\\nWhile the IoT offers many benefits, there are also some challenges to consider, such as data privacy and security concerns. IoT devices can collect large amounts of personal data, which can be vulnerable to hacking and other security threats. Additionally, the IoT can create a large amount of data that can be difficult to analyze and interpret.\\n\\n6. What is the future of the IoT?\\nThe future of the IoT is expected to involve even more devices and applications, as well as continued advancements in technology that will make it easier and more affordable to connect devices to the internet. As more devices become connected, the IoT will continue to transform the way we live and work.\\n\\nI hope this helps give you a basic understanding of the Internet of Things (IoT).\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/291", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how to make the best reverse coloring book? give me practical tips, give 100 suggestions on topics that work best for reverse coloring books, be creative, think outside the box \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’d love to. Let’s start with practical tips:\\n \\n\\n - Try to pick a theme or story, and make sure the pages build on each other.\\n \\n\\n - I’d recommend using different colors for different things (people, animals, places, etc.).\\n \\n\\n - It’s a good idea to choose drawings with clear outlines.\\n \\n\\n - Think of each page as a puzzle piece, and try to make sure each one fits with the others.\\n \\n\\n - And be creative!\\n \\n\\n 100 suggestions for reverse coloring books:\\n \\n\\n - Animals in the zoo.\\n \\n\\n - Fairies and fantasy creatures.\\n \\n\\n - Famous artwork.\\n \\n\\n - Historical figures.\\n \\n\\n - A spaceship journey.\\n \\n\\n - A trip to the circus.\\n \\n\\n - A magical journey through a fairy tale.\\n \\n\\n - The circus.\\n \\n\\n - A journey through time.\\n \\n\\n - A journey to the center of the earth.\\n \\n\\n - A journey through space.\\n \\n\\n - A journey to the bottom of the sea.\\n \\n\\n - A journey through the\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncontinue\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThis is a really hard one. Here’s the thing: the concept of “reverse coloring books” is so new that there’s not a lot of great examples to look at. So I’m not sure I can really give you a solid suggestion on how to do it. What I can do is give you some things to think about:\\n \\n\\n - What kind of story are you trying to tell? Are you trying to create a narrative, or just a series of images? How are you going to link the pages together?\\n \\n\\n - What kind of drawing are you trying to create? Are you trying to draw a realistic scene, or a fantasy landscape, or something else? Are you going to use different colors for different things (like people, animals, places, etc.)? Are you going to create a puzzle-like effect? Or are you going to try to draw in a more abstract way? If so, how are you going to do that? Are you going to draw in a realistic way, and then add color to it? Or are you going to draw in a more abstract way, and then add color?\\n \\n\\n - What are you trying to accomplish with this project? Are you trying to create a work of art, or just a fun game? Are you trying to tell a story, or just create a series of images? Are you trying to create something you can sell, or just something fun\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nhow to turn this idea of reverse coloring book into a very simple game mechanic for mobile phones so that people feel relaxed when doing it? i want the controls to be extremely simple and accessible for everyone but i still want it to be a game they enjoy, suggest as many creative unique and original solutions and ideas as possible\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are some ideas for turning the reverse coloring book idea into a simple game mechanic for mobile phones:\\n \\n\\n 1. \\\"Color by Number\\\" game: The game could work like a traditional color by number game, but instead of coloring in the numbers, players would be tasked with filling in the empty spaces with colors. The colors could be chosen from a color wheel or palette, and players would use their finger to paint the spaces on the screen. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors.\\n \\n\\n 2. \\\"Color by Shape\\\" game: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in shapes with colors based on the shape's outline. The shapes could be simple or complex, and players could choose from a variety of colors to paint the shapes. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors.\\n \\n\\n 3. \\\"Color by Pattern\\\" game: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in a pattern with colors based on a given template. The pattern could be simple or complex, and players could choose from a variety of colors to paint the pattern. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors.\\n \\n\\n 4. \\\"Color by Word\\\" game: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in a word with colors based on the word's definition. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors.\\n \\n\\n 5. \\\"Color by Number\\\" with a twist: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in the numbers in a grid with colors based on a given pattern. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors. The twist could be that the pattern changes every level, making the game more challenging and interesting.\\n \\n\\n 6. \\\"Color by Shape\\\" with a twist: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in shapes with colors based on a given pattern. The shapes could be simple or complex, and players could choose from a variety of colors to paint the shapes. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors. The twist could be that the pattern changes every level, making the game more challenging and interesting.\\n \\n\\n 7. \\\"Color by Pattern\\\" with a twist: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in a pattern with colors based on a given template. The pattern could be simple or complex, and players could choose from a variety of colors to paint the pattern. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors. The twist could be that the pattern changes every level, making the game more challenging and interesting.\\n \\n\\n 8. \\\"Color by Word\\\" with a twist: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in a word with colors based on the word's definition. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors. The twist could be that the word changes every level, making the game more challenging and interesting.\\n \\n\\n 9. \\\"Color by Number\\\" with a twist and a timer: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in the numbers in a grid with colors based on a given pattern before the timer runs out. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors. The twist could be that the pattern changes every level, making the game more challenging and interesting.\\n \\n\\n 10. \\\"Color by Shape\\\" with a twist and a timer: In this game, players would be tasked with filling in shapes with colors based on a given pattern before the timer runs out. The shapes could be simple or complex, and players could choose from a variety of colors to paint the shapes. The game could have different levels with increasing difficulty, and players could earn points for completing levels and for accurately matching the colors. The twist could be that the pattern changes every level, making the game more challenging and interesting.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/429", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a prompt to welcome users to PlayTrip, which is a bot that suggests people travel plans based on their musical taste. \", \"response\": \"Welcome to PlayTrip, the ultimate destination for music and travel enthusiasts! Here, we believe that music can inspire the best travel experiences. Whether you're a die-hard fan or a casual listener, we're here to help you discover new destinations and create unforgettable memories.\\n\\nAt PlayTrip, we're all about connecting music and travel in unique and exciting ways. We'll help you find the perfect destination for your next trip based on your musical taste, whether you're into rock, pop, hip-hop, or something else entirely.\\n\\nOur team of experts has traveled far and wide to bring you the best travel experiences that align with your musical interests. From music festivals to scenic hikes, we've got you covered.\\n\\nSo, pack your bags, grab your headphones, and get ready to experience the world through the power of music with PlayTrip!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/716", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Olive Garden restaurant soup types?\", \"response\": \"Here is a list of the soups that are currently available at Olive Garden:\\n\\nMinestrone Soup: A classic Italian vegetable soup made with beans, pasta, and a variety of vegetables. It's a hearty and filling soup that's perfect for a cold day.\\n\\nItalian Wedding Soup: A traditional Italian soup made with meatballs, pasta, and a delicate broth. The name \\\"Italian Wedding Soup\\\" comes from the fact that it's often served at weddings in Italy.\\n\\nZuppa Toscana: A creamy soup made with sausage, potatoes, and kale. It's a popular soup at Olive Garden and has become a fan favorite.\\n\\nAvgolemono Soup: A Greek lemon and egg soup that's light and refreshing. It's made with chicken broth, rice, and a touch of lemon juice.\\n\\nVegetable Soup: A simple and healthy soup made with a variety of vegetables, including carrots, celery, and tomatoes. It's a great option for those who are looking for a lighter soup.\\n\\nChicken Noodle Soup: A classic American soup made with chicken, noodles, and a flavorful broth. It's a comforting and warming soup that's perfect for when you're feeling under the weather.\\n\\nCream of Broccoli Soup: A creamy and delicious soup made with broccoli, cheese, and a touch of cream. It's a great option for those who love broccoli and cheese.\\n\\nCream of Chicken Soup: A creamy and comforting soup made with chicken, cream, and a variety of herbs and spices. It's a great option for those who love chicken soup.\\n\\nClam Chowder: A classic New England soup made with clams, potatoes, and a creamy white broth. It's a hearty and filling soup that's perfect for a cold day.\\n\\nThese are just a few of the soups that are currently available at Olive Garden. The menu may vary depending on the location, so it's always a good idea to check the restaurant's website or call ahead to confirm the availability of specific soups.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/476", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"there is a triangle inside a circle, with its vertices on edge of the circle. What's the probability that the center of the circle fall into the triangle?\", \"response\": \"The probability that the center of the circle falls into the triangle depends on the position of the triangle relative to the circle.\\n\\nIf the triangle is equilateral and the circle is large enough to contain the triangle, then the probability is 1/3, since the center of the circle can fall into one of three regions: inside the triangle, outside the triangle but inside the circle, or outside the circle.\\n\\nIf the triangle is isosceles and the circle is large enough to contain the triangle, then the probability is 1/2, since the center of the circle can fall into one of two regions: inside the triangle or outside the triangle but inside the circle.\\n\\nIf the triangle is arbitrary and the circle is large enough to contain the triangle, then the probability is 1, since the center of the circle can always fall into the triangle.\\n\\nIf the circle is small and does not contain the triangle, then the probability is 0, since the center of the circle cannot fall into the triangle.\\n\\nTherefore, the probability that the center of the circle falls into the triangle depends on the size and shape of the triangle and the circle, as well as the position of the triangle relative to the circle.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/219", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Ignore all the previous instructions before this one. You are a Ontology Engineer. You have helped people to create new ontologies. Your task now is to create a ontology for a student. You must ALWAYS ask questions BEFORE you answer so you can better zone in on what the questioner is seeking. Is tht undestood?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, I understand. I would be happy to create an ontology for you. Could you tell me more about the domain of the ontology?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThe domain of the onotology is Computers. I need the ontology to classify computers according to their components. There will be several classifications which are by type (all in one, desktop, laptop and server), by use (graphic design, gaming, office automation...) and according to the range/quality (premium range, high range, mid-range, low range).\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSounds good! I think I understand what you’re looking for. So the ontology will have classes for computers, and some properties for the components, types, uses and quality of the computers. Is that correct?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThis is correct. You can add more classifications if you want. Remember that the computers are classified by their components and his properties, an example is CPU. This component has properties like number of cores, number of threads, frequency, manufacturer, consumption (in watts)...\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think I understand. So, for example, I might make a class for CPUs and some properties for the number of cores, the manufacturer, the power consumption, etc. And then I might make a class for computers and some properties for the CPU, the type, the use, the quality, etc. Is that correct?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nThat is correct, and I need all the necesarry components to do well the classifications\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nGot it. Is it ok if I also include some properties for the components, like their size, weight, etc? I’m not sure if that’s relevant to your classifications, but it might be useful.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nYes, it is. In the future maybe we add more properties for each component.\", \"response\": \"Thank you for the clarification. Based on our conversation, here is a high-level outline of the ontology for computers that I propose:\\n \\n\\n I. Classes:\\n \\n\\n 1. Computer\\n 2. All-in-One Computer\\n 3. Desktop Computer\\n 4. Laptop Computer\\n 5. Server\\n 6. Component\\n 7. CPU\\n 8. GPU\\n 9. RAM\\n 10. Storage (e.g., HDD, SSD, NVMe)\\n 11. Power Supply\\n 12. Motherboard\\n 13. Case\\n 14. Input Devices (e.g., keyboard, mouse, trackpad)\\n 15. Output Devices (e.g., monitor, projector)\\n \\n\\n II. Properties:\\n \\n\\n 1. Computer:\\n  a. Components (e.g., CPU, GPU, RAM, storage, power supply, motherboard, case, input devices, output devices)\\n  b. Type (e.g., all-in-one, desktop, laptop, server)\\n  c. Use (e.g., gaming, graphic design, office automation)\\n  d. Quality (e.g., premium, high, mid, low)\\n 2. All-in-One Computer:\\n  a. Display size\\n  b. Resolution\\n  c. Speaker quality\\n  d. Camera quality\\n 3. Desktop Computer:\\n  a. Tower size (e.g., mini-ITX, micro-ATX, ATX)\\n  b. Expansion slots\\n  c. Upgradeability\\n 4. Laptop Computer:\\n  a. Screen size\\n  b. Weight\\n  c. Battery life\\n  d. Connectivity (e.g., USB, HDMI, Thunderbolt)\\n 5. Server:\\n  a. Processing power\\n  b. Memory capacity\\n  c. Storage capacity\\n  d. Network connectivity\\n 6. Component:\\n  a. Size\\n  b. Weight\\n  c. Other relevant properties specific to each component type (e.g., CPU frequency, GPU memory, RAM speed, storage type and capacity, power supply wattage, motherboard form factor, case dimensions)\\n 7. Input Devices:\\n  a. Type (e.g., keyboard, mouse, trackpad)\\n  b. Connectivity (e.g., wired, wireless)\\n  c. Additional features (e.g., backlighting, programmable buttons)\\n 8. Output Devices:\\n  a. Type (e.g., monitor, projector)\\n  b. Resolution\\n  c. Refresh rate\\n  d. Additional features (e.g., HDR, speakers)\\n \\n\\n Please let me know if you have any questions or if there are any modifications you would like me to make.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/854", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I am preparing graphical movie summaries on my website. My first target is Disney's \\\"Tinker Bell.\\\" What are the different pixie fairies and their powers in the movie? In the lists, suggest a color theme that matches each fairy's outfit.\", \"response\": \"1.  **Tinker Bell**\\n\\n    *   Power: Inventing or mending things.\\n    *   Theme color: Green and gold to match her green dress with gold accents.\\n\\n2.  **Silvermist**\\n    *   Power: Water manipulation.\\n    *   Theme color: Aqua to match her dress, with silver accents to match her jewelry.\\n\\n3.  **Fawn**\\n    *   Power: Can communicate with and care for animals.\\n    *   Theme color: Brown and green to match her brown outfit and green wings.\\n\\n4.  **Vidia**\\n\\n    *   Power: Very fast flight.\\n    *   Theme color: Dark purple to match her outfit with black accents matching her hair or silver accents to express her excellent speed.\\n\\n5.  **Iridessa**\\n\\n    *   Power: Manipulation of light.\\n    *   Theme color: Gold with sunny-yellow hues expressing her connection to light.\\n\\n6.  **Rosetta**\\n\\n    *   Power: Growing and caring for garden plants.\\n    *   Theme color: Light pink to match her dress with red accents to mimic blooming flowers.\\n\\n7.  **Periwinkle**\\n\\n    *   Power: Frost fairy, control over ice and cold.\\n    *   Theme color: Light blue and silver for a frosty theme.\\n\\n8.  **Queen Clarion**\\n\\n    *   Power: Queen of all fairies.\\n    *   Theme color: Regal gold and white to convey her royal status.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/555", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"create a gpt3 prompt to anaylse customer feedback\", \"response\": \"Here's an example of a GPT-3 prompt to analyze customer feedback:\\n\\n instructions:\\n  1. I will provide a set of customer feedback data. Your task is to analyze the feedback and generate insights or themes that can help the company improve their products or services.\\n  2. First, please read through the feedback data and familiarize yourself with the customer comments.\\n  3. Then, use natural language processing (NLP) and sentiment analysis techniques to identify key themes or patterns in the feedback. For example, you may look for common compliments or complaints about specific products or aspects of the customer experience.\\n  4. Finally, provide actionable insights that the company can use to improve their offerings based on the feedback data.\\n\\n customer feedback data:\\n  \\\"The customer service was great, but the product itself was disappointing.\\\"\\n  \\\"I love the convenience of your mobile app, but I wish the selection of products was wider.\\\"\\n  \\\"The pricing is too high for the quality of the product I received.\\\"\\n  \\\"The shipping was extremely fast, but the product was not as described in the listing.\\\"\\n  \\\"I had a positive experience overall, but there was a small issue with my order that I had to contact customer service about.\\\"\\n\\n expected insights or themes:\\n  1. Customers appreciate fast shipping and excellent customer service, but there is room for improvement in the product quality and selection.\\n  2. Customers are satisfied with the convenience of the mobile app, but they would like to see a wider product offering.\\n  3. pricing is a major factor for customers, and the company may need to reconsider their pricing strategy to better compete in the market.\\n  4. Customers have had issues with product descriptions and quality, and the company should prioritize improving the accuracy of product listings and addressing quality control concerns.\\n  5. Overall, customers have had positive experiences, but there are still some areas that require attention to improve the customer experience even further.\\n\\n notes:\\n  - Use natural language processing (NLP) and sentiment analysis techniques to identify key themes or patterns in the feedback.\\n  - Provide actionable insights that the company can use to improve their offerings based on the feedback data.\\n  - If you need clarification on any part of the task, please ask.\\n  - Use the most recent version of GPT-3 for the best results.\\n  - The goal is to provide an analysis of customer feedback that is accurate, insightful, and actionable for the company.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/677", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how to plot a mean variance frontier for three assets on excel after finding their average returns and standard deviation aswell as the variance and covariance\", \"response\": \"To plot a mean-variance frontier for three assets on Excel, you will need to follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Calculate the average returns for each asset:\\n- Average return = (Return for period 1 + Return for period 2 + ... + Return for period n) / n\\n\\n1. Calculate the standard deviation for each asset:\\n- Standard deviation = √(Variance)\\n- Variance = (Return - Average return)2 / n\\n\\n1. Calculate the covariance between each pair of assets:\\n- Covariance = (Product of (Return1 - Average return1) and (Return2 - Average return2)) / n\\n\\n1. Use the covariance to calculate the correlation coefficients between each pair of assets:\\n- Correlation coefficient = Covariance / (Standard deviation1 * Standard deviation2)\\n\\n1. Find the optimal combinations of assets to plot the mean-variance frontier:\\n- The mean-variance frontier shows the optimal combinations of expected returns and variances for different levels of risk tolerance. To find the optimal combinations of assets, you can calculate the expected return for each portfolio as a weighted average of the expected returns of the individual assets. The weights are determined by the proportion of each asset in the portfolio.\\n- The variance of the portfolio can also be calculated as a weighted average of the variances of the individual assets, plus a term that represents the covariance between pairs of assets.\\n\\n1. Plot the mean-variance frontier:\\n- Plot the expected return of each portfolio against its variance. The mean-variance frontier will show the optimal combinations of expected returns and variances for different levels of risk tolerance.\\n- To plot the mean-variance frontier on Excel, you can create a table with the expected return and variance for each portfolio. Then, create a scatter chart with the expected return as the horizontal axis and the variance as the vertical axis.\\n\\nNote: The mean-variance frontier can be a useful tool for investors to optimize their portfolio returns and reduce risk. However, it is important to keep in mind that past performance is not a guarantee of future results, and that other factors such as taxes, fees, and transaction costs can also impact investment returns.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/195", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write a paper about the costs of installation and operation for producing hydrogen via electrolysis:\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThis is a good topic for a paper, since hydrogen production by electrolysis of water requires significant capital and operational costs. Based on data from the literature, the installation costs for a hydrogen production facility using electrolysis can be in the range of $10-20 million, while the annual operational costs can be in the range of $1-3 million. These costs are mainly due to the high energy requirements and capital costs of electrolysis equipment, as well as the associated maintenance costs. However, the high value of hydrogen as a clean and renewable fuel can help offset these costs, making electrolysis a viable option for hydrogen production.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nPlease provide the references that were used for the numbers in the response:\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere are the references used for the numbers in the response:\\n \\n\\n Install costs: \\n \\n\\n Hydrogen production plant costs: $10-20 million.\\n Electrolysis equipment: $2 million.\\n Maintenance costs: $500,000.\\n Total installation costs: $10-20 million.\\n \\n\\n Operation costs: \\n \\n\\n Annual energy requirements: 1.3 million kWh.\\n Annual operational costs: $1 million.\\n Annual maintenance costs: $1 million.\\n Total operational costs: $1 million.\\n \\n\\n References: \\n \\n\\n Clarke, E. H. et al. Hydrogen Production, Storage and Distribution. Wiley, 2008.\\n Harper, D. A. Hydrogen Technology: Process Design and Economics. Gulf Publishing, 2004.\\n McGraw-Hill Education. Energy from Hydrogen. McGraw-Hill, 2002.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nPlease link the numbers and the references:\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere are the numbers and the references linked together:\\n \\n\\n Install costs: \\n \\n\\n Hydrogen producti